            'Lighting is a powerful tool in theatre that helps to create a mood, set the scene, and highlight important elements of the story. It can be used to create a fantasy world, like a place made entirely of light, where anything is possible. The use of light and shadow has been experimented with since ancient times, and today\'s stage lighting technology allows designers to shape colours, moods, and emotions. This technology has come a long way, from using simple props and puppets to sophisticated modern technology.',
            'There are different types of lights used in theatre, including floodlights, PARs, and profiles, each with its own unique characteristics and uses. Floodlights are simple and provide a broad beam of light, while PARs produce a more intense, oval-shaped beam. Profiles offer the most control over the light and can be used to project patterns and textures onto the stage. These lights can be used to create a variety of effects, from highlighting specific areas of the stage to creating a sense of depth and atmosphere.',
