              text: 'The deeper you delve into this knowledge, the more you create innovatively. This is when dance ( nṛitya ) becomes ‘ Nitya Nūtana aur Purātana ’, meaning it is simultaneously old, yet can always bring newness. Now, let us rediscover nṛitya ! Discover joy NṚITYA Align your body and mind Nurture your spirit and culture Create and choreograph Express and explore Fig. 10.1. Elements of dance 10_Ch10 Dance.indd 10_Ch10 Dance.indd Madhurima Fig. 10.2. A dance performance by the students What Constitutes a Dance Movement? For dancers, the body is a medium through which all movement comes alive. Since dance begins in the body, its alignment, balance, and graceful control shape the strength and clarity of every movement. Proper body posture forms the foundation of all technique and helps prevent injuries that arise from incorrect alignment. Just as in any physical activity, in dance too, warming up prepares the muscles and joints, ensuring that movements are free, fluid, and safe. In Indian dances, this physical awareness is deepened through a conscious harmony between breath and body, allowing dancers to sense and direct the flow of energy within, similar to yoga. A well-aligned body allows the free flow of energy, enhancing endurance, stamina, and emotional expression. Before learning any dance movement, a dancer must first understand how to hold the body correctly. Now, let us experience how awareness of body alignment transforms an ordinary movement into a stylised dance movement — almost like a sculpture coming to life! Fig. 10.3. Flow in dance Where there is a body, there is dance. Dance begins not with perfection, but with sensitivity to the body. Thus, it is dance itself that awakens the dancer.',
