              text: 'Now that you have gone through the essential warm-up activities like sketching and journalling, get ready for exploring the next level of Visual Art. The choice of materials, tools, and techniques has shaped every artist’s expression throughout history. Think of the range of surfaces and materials from the prehistoric cave paintings made with earth pigments to the digital drawing devices of today! Many artworks have survived changing weather and climatic conditions as well as other external threats and damage. The fact that we can still see and experience artworks that were made thousands of years ago proves that artists had deep knowledge and advanced techniques of using various materials in art processes. Let us recall Some pottery and metal casting techniques that are practised today are more than 5,000 years old. Talking About Mediums The word ‘ medium ’ is a common term that refers to the materials, tools, and processes used in making visual artwork. Fig. 15.1. Visual arts mediums and materials for drawing and painting, printmaking, sculpture, textile crafts, paper crafts, and digital art Mediums and Techniques in Visual Art 15_Ch VA.indd 15_Ch VA.indd (Sukhbir joins Sharmila and Samir. His hands, face, and clothes are full of charcoal stains.) It is fun, Sharmila. We are learning about painting mediums , and I like watercolours on paper . Samir, how are you enjoying the Visual Arts classes? Which mediums have you tried so far? I have painted on canvas, but not on cloth. Some day I would like to paint a wall mural. Really? Could I go with you... When will you visit next? I enjoy sculpture because it lets me touch and shape things with my hands.',
